# Eval engineering

Before marking a coding task complete:

1. Run `node "$GARISEK_OS_ROOT/tools/eval-engineering/cursor-eval.mjs" --root . --fast`
2. On failure: fix or report — do not claim done.
3. Cross-cutting refactors: use `--full` instead of `--fast`.
4. **Floor stations / overlay shell:** after edits to any
   `SCAN_STATION_OVERLAY_COHORT` workspace, run
   `pnpm run eval:station <id>` (see `docs/eval/README.md`). SoT is the
   full cohort — peers, not Pack/Unbox-as-golden. Display eval is
   **slot-table only** — there is no `eval:cohort overlay`. Do not delete
   cohort-law `visibility` / `zIndex.panel` styles to silence critique.
5. **Slot-table cohort (the only display eval):** after CompoundItem /
   `useSlotTableLayout` / PRODUCT_TABLES / DataTable funnel engine edits, run
   `pnpm run eval:cohort slot-table`. SoT is engine + every product table peer
   — not To-ship alone. Hand-model leftovers:
   `pnpm run eval:discover` — delete only listed DELETE ids; never KEEP rows.
6. **Shortcut-display cohort:** after `?` / shortcut / TableStatusBar hotkey
   edits, run `pnpm run eval:cohort shortcuts`. Staff `?` reveals letters
   inline on the buttons. Standing keycaps: refuse. Cheat sheet from the
   table-foot `?`: refuse. No `title`/popover on the question-mark.
7. **SKU-identity cohort (identity, not display):** after any edit to a
   product title, SKU or photo read/write, run
   `pnpm run eval:cohort sku-identity`. SoT is the **Zoho item**, and the
   cohort is the whole peer set (`SKU_IDENTITY_PEERS`) — a fix proven on one
   desk and not its peers is the drift this cohort reports. Gate `Sku identity`
   (`always`) in `verify:fast`; CLI `npx tsx scripts/sku-identity-guard.ts`.
   Re-adding the deleted `similarity(product_title, …) >= 0.25` join gate to
   silence a bad title: refuse — fix the write side
   (`skuCatalogNoZohoTwinPredicateSql`). Spelling a new `||` title ladder
   instead of `resolveSkuIdentityTitle`: refuse. Known debt is shrink-only.

Verify commands come from this repo's `package.json` — not model-invented commands.
